{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42574",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "apko dirFS has a symlink-following path traversal that allows multiple entry points to escape the build root"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "apko allows users to build and publish OCI container images built from apk packages. From version 0.14.8 to before version 1.2.5, a crafted .apk could install a TypeSymlink tar entry whose target pointed outside the build root, and a subsequent directory-creation or file-write entry in the same or later archive could traverse that symlink to reach host paths the build user could write to. This issue has been patched in version 1.2.5."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42574",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42574\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: chainguard.dev/apko\nFixed Version: 1.2.5\nLink: [CVE-2026-42574](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42574)\napko allows users to build and publish OCI container images built from apk packages. From version 0.14.8 to before version 1.2.5, a crafted .apk could install a TypeSymlink tar entry whose target pointed outside the build root, and a subsequent directory-creation or file-write entry in the same or later archive could traverse that symlink to reach host paths the build user could write to. This issue has been patched in version 1.2.5.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42574**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|chainguard.dev/apko|1.2.5|[CVE-2026-42574](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42574)|\n\napko allows users to build and publish OCI container images built from apk packages. From version 0.14.8 to before version 1.2.5, a crafted .apk could install a TypeSymlink tar entry whose target pointed outside the build root, and a subsequent directory-creation or file-write entry in the same or later archive could traverse that symlink to reach host paths the build user could write to. This issue has been patched in version 1.2.5."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42575",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "apko doesn't verify downloaded apk packages against APKINDEX checksum (package substitution possible)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "apko allows users to build and publish OCI container images built from apk packages. Prior to version 1.2.7, apko verifies the signature on APKINDEX.tar.gz but never compares individually downloaded .apk packages against the checksum recorded in the signed index. The checksum is parsed and available via ChecksumString(), and the downloaded package control hash is computed, but the two values are never compared in getPackageImpl(). Mismatched packages are silently accepted. An attacker who can substitute download responses (compromised mirror, HTTP repository, poisoned CDN cache) can install arbitrary packages into built images. This issue has been patched in version 1.2.7."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42575",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42575\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: chainguard.dev/apko\nFixed Version: 1.2.7\nLink: [CVE-2026-42575](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42575)\napko allows users to build and publish OCI container images built from apk packages. Prior to version 1.2.7, apko verifies the signature on APKINDEX.tar.gz but never compares individually downloaded .apk packages against the checksum recorded in the signed index. The checksum is parsed and available via ChecksumString(), and the downloaded package control hash is computed, but the two values are never compared in getPackageImpl(). Mismatched packages are silently accepted. An attacker who can substitute download responses (compromised mirror, HTTP repository, poisoned CDN cache) can install arbitrary packages into built images. This issue has been patched in version 1.2.7.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42575**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|chainguard.dev/apko|1.2.7|[CVE-2026-42575](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42575)|\n\napko allows users to build and publish OCI container images built from apk packages. Prior to version 1.2.7, apko verifies the signature on APKINDEX.tar.gz but never compares individually downloaded .apk packages against the checksum recorded in the signed index. The checksum is parsed and available via ChecksumString(), and the downloaded package control hash is computed, but the two values are never compared in getPackageImpl(). Mismatched packages are silently accepted. An attacker who can substitute download responses (compromised mirror, HTTP repository, poisoned CDN cache) can install arbitrary packages into built images. This issue has been patched in version 1.2.7."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42576",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "apko `DiscoverKeys` has a panic on non-rsa jwks key that causes crash during key discovery"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "apko allows users to build and publish OCI container images built from apk packages. Prior to version 1.2.7, DiscoverKeys in pkg/apk/apk/implementation.go unconditionally type-asserts JWKS keys as *rsa.PublicKey without checking the key type. If a repository JWKS endpoint returns a non-RSA key (e.g. EC), the unchecked assertion panics and crashes apko. This affects any workflow that initializes the APK database and fetches repository keys. This issue has been patched in version 1.2.7."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42576",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42576\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: chainguard.dev/apko\nFixed Version: 1.2.7\nLink: [CVE-2026-42576](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42576)\napko allows users to build and publish OCI container images built from apk packages. Prior to version 1.2.7, DiscoverKeys in pkg/apk/apk/implementation.go unconditionally type-asserts JWKS keys as *rsa.PublicKey without checking the key type. If a repository JWKS endpoint returns a non-RSA key (e.g. EC), the unchecked assertion panics and crashes apko. This affects any workflow that initializes the APK database and fetches repository keys. This issue has been patched in version 1.2.7.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42576**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|chainguard.dev/apko|1.2.7|[CVE-2026-42576](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42576)|\n\napko allows users to build and publish OCI container images built from apk packages. Prior to version 1.2.7, DiscoverKeys in pkg/apk/apk/implementation.go unconditionally type-asserts JWKS keys as *rsa.PublicKey without checking the key type. If a repository JWKS endpoint returns a non-RSA key (e.g. EC), the unchecked assertion panics and crashes apko. This affects any workflow that initializes the APK database and fetches repository keys. This issue has been patched in version 1.2.7."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-26958",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "filippo.io/edwards25519: filippo.io/edwards25519: Cryptographic integrity bypass due to incorrect MultiScalarMult results"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "filippo.io/edwards25519 is a Go library implementing the edwards25519 elliptic curve with APIs for building cryptographic primitives. In versions 1.1.0 and earlier, MultiScalarMult produces invalid results or undefined behavior if the receiver is not the identity point. If (*Point).MultiScalarMult is called on an initialized point that is not the identity point, it returns an incorrect result. If the method is called on an uninitialized point, the behavior is undefined. In particular, if the receiver is the zero value, MultiScalarMult returns an invalid point that compares Equal to every other point. Note that MultiScalarMult is a rarely used, advanced API. For example, users who depend on filippo.io/edwards25519 only through github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql are not affected. This issue has been fixed in version 1.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-26958",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-26958\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: filippo.io/edwards25519\nFixed Version: 1.1.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-26958](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-26958)\nfilippo.io/edwards25519 is a Go library implementing the edwards25519 elliptic curve with APIs for building cryptographic primitives. In versions 1.1.0 and earlier, MultiScalarMult produces invalid results or undefined behavior if the receiver is not the identity point. If (*Point).MultiScalarMult is called on an initialized point that is not the identity point, it returns an incorrect result. If the method is called on an uninitialized point, the behavior is undefined. In particular, if the receiver is the zero value, MultiScalarMult returns an invalid point that compares Equal to every other point. Note that MultiScalarMult is a rarely used, advanced API. For example, users who depend on filippo.io/edwards25519 only through github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql are not affected. This issue has been fixed in version 1.1.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-26958**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|filippo.io/edwards25519|1.1.1|[CVE-2026-26958](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-26958)|\n\nfilippo.io/edwards25519 is a Go library implementing the edwards25519 elliptic curve with APIs for building cryptographic primitives. In versions 1.1.0 and earlier, MultiScalarMult produces invalid results or undefined behavior if the receiver is not the identity point. If (*Point).MultiScalarMult is called on an initialized point that is not the identity point, it returns an incorrect result. If the method is called on an uninitialized point, the behavior is undefined. In particular, if the receiver is the zero value, MultiScalarMult returns an invalid point that compares Equal to every other point. Note that MultiScalarMult is a rarely used, advanced API. For example, users who depend on filippo.io/edwards25519 only through github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql are not affected. This issue has been fixed in version 1.1.1."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 1.7,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-1229",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CIRCL has an incorrect calculation in secp384r1 CombinedMult"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The CombinedMult function in the CIRCL ecc/p384 package (secp384r1 curve) produces an incorrect value for specific inputs. The issue is fixed by using complete addition formulas.\nECDH and ECDSA signing relying on this curve are not affected.\n\nThe bug was fixed in  v1.6.3 https://github.com/cloudflare/circl/releases/tag/v1.6.3 ."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-1229",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-1229\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: github.com/cloudflare/circl\nFixed Version: 1.6.3\nLink: [CVE-2026-1229](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-1229)\nThe CombinedMult function in the CIRCL ecc/p384 package (secp384r1 curve) produces an incorrect value for specific inputs. The issue is fixed by using complete addition formulas.\nECDH and ECDSA signing relying on this curve are not affected.\n\nThe bug was fixed in  v1.6.3 https://github.com/cloudflare/circl/releases/tag/v1.6.3 .",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-1229**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|github.com/cloudflare/circl|1.6.3|[CVE-2026-1229](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-1229)|\n\nThe CombinedMult function in the CIRCL ecc/p384 package (secp384r1 curve) produces an incorrect value for specific inputs. The issue is fixed by using complete addition formulas.\nECDH and ECDSA signing relying on this curve are not affected.\n\nThe bug was fixed in  v1.6.3 https://github.com/cloudflare/circl/releases/tag/v1.6.3 ."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 2.9,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:L/SI:L/SA:L/E:P/S:N/AU:Y/U:Amber",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-46680",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/containerd/containerd: containerd: Privilege escalation via incorrect user ID handling"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "containerd is an open-source container runtime. In versions prior to 1.7.32, 2.0.9, 2.2.4 and 2.3.1, containers launched with a numeric User directive that cannot be parsed as a 32-bit integer are incorrectly treated as a username, leading to runAsNonRoot evasion. If a crafted image provides an /etc/passwd file mapping this large numeric string to root, the container ultimately runs as root (UID 0). This allows the Kubernetes runAsNonRoot restriction to be bypassed, causing unexpected behavior for environments that require containers to run as a non-root user. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.32, 2.0.9, 2.2.4 and 2.3.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46680",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-46680\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/containerd/containerd/v2\nFixed Version: 2.0.9, 2.2.4, 2.3.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-46680](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46680)\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. In versions prior to 1.7.32, 2.0.9, 2.2.4 and 2.3.1, containers launched with a numeric User directive that cannot be parsed as a 32-bit integer are incorrectly treated as a username, leading to runAsNonRoot evasion. If a crafted image provides an /etc/passwd file mapping this large numeric string to root, the container ultimately runs as root (UID 0). This allows the Kubernetes runAsNonRoot restriction to be bypassed, causing unexpected behavior for environments that require containers to run as a non-root user. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.32, 2.0.9, 2.2.4 and 2.3.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-46680**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/containerd/containerd/v2|2.0.9, 2.2.4, 2.3.1|[CVE-2026-46680](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46680)|\n\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. In versions prior to 1.7.32, 2.0.9, 2.2.4 and 2.3.1, containers launched with a numeric User directive that cannot be parsed as a 32-bit integer are incorrectly treated as a username, leading to runAsNonRoot evasion. If a crafted image provides an /etc/passwd file mapping this large numeric string to root, the container ultimately runs as root (UID 0). This allows the Kubernetes runAsNonRoot restriction to be bypassed, causing unexpected behavior for environments that require containers to run as a non-root user. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.32, 2.0.9, 2.2.4 and 2.3.1."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 7.3,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53488",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/containerd/containerd: containerd: Host-root command execution via unvalidated image config labels in CRI plugin"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "containerd is an open-source container runtime. In versions prior to 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10 the CRI plugin propagates labels from an image config (LABEL instruction in Dockerfile) to a container without validation. This may result in executing an arbitrary command on the host, via a plugin that consumes container labels for some operations. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53488",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53488\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/containerd/containerd/v2\nFixed Version: 2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5, 2.3.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-53488](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53488)\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. In versions prior to 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10 the CRI plugin propagates labels from an image config (LABEL instruction in Dockerfile) to a container without validation. This may result in executing an arbitrary command on the host, via a plugin that consumes container labels for some operations. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53488**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/containerd/containerd/v2|2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5, 2.3.2|[CVE-2026-53488](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53488)|\n\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. In versions prior to 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10 the CRI plugin propagates labels from an image config (LABEL instruction in Dockerfile) to a container without validation. This may result in executing an arbitrary command on the host, via a plugin that consumes container labels for some operations. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10."
              },
              "properties": {
